    {
      "caption": "Pyramid of energy: the 10% rule",
      "duration_ms": 11000,
      "id": "s3",
      "narration": "Draw biomass or energy per trophic level and you get a pyramid. Only about one tenth of the energy at one level becomes the next — the rest is lost in respiration, movement, and egestion. That is why food chains stay short: there is rarely enough energy left for a sixth level.",
