    {
      "caption": "Misconception: energy is recycled",
      "duration_ms": 9000,
      "id": "s6",
      "narration": "A common mix-up: energy is not recycled in ecosystems. Energy flows one way — in as sunlight, out as heat — and must be constantly resupplied. What is recycled is matter: carbon, nitrogen and water loop around again and again.",
